ЅЅ√6JЁnџЁf№е ␀|оАgzоАWнR“Lб√6Jб~АлzоАWнRЏ6JЁnёЁfяF␀нR“6J*^†␀ЈнR Ќ\*^†ЁuўЁtЏ*^†#"^†ЁnўЁfЏ^ЬеЁnџЁf№]бsЁnџЁf№еA␀|оАgzоАWнR“ГLббZАлzоАWнR8Ё~џ∆ Ёwџ0Ё4№ЁnёЁfяЁuўЁtЏЁ4ё Ё4яЁnўЁfЏлЁnЁfеЁnџЁf№е—бs√6JЁщЁб…Ќ÷
!пЪеЌЃЅ!␀␀’еЌ	
ЅЅ!ыЪеЌЃЅ√\West of the House␀Entrance Hall␀Dusty Library␀Stone Cellar␀Quiet Crypt␀Portrait Gallery␀Treasure Vault␀Walled Garden␀Clock Tower␀Abandoned Kitchen␀Pantry␀Mechanic's Workshop␀Overgrown Orchard␀Ruined Greenhouse␀Bottom of the Well␀Echoing Tunnel␀Pump Room␀Underground Reservoir␀Tidal Shrine␀Clockwork Guardroom␀Bridge of Gears␀Crystal Mine␀Sealed Archive␀Star Observatory␀The House of Tides has stood still since its keeper vanished. An empty cabinet awaits three lost treasures: idol, chalice and crown. The house is east; its garden is north.␀Rain has stained the hall's patterned tiles. A hook hangs beside the front door west. The kitchen is north, the library east; stone steps descend to the cellar.␀Shelves crowd a table covered in the keeper's notes. A passage leads north to the archive. A margin reads: 'Silver opens the old way; brass guards the idol.' The hall lies west.␀Dust softens the stone floor. The crypt lies north, a mechanic's workshop west. Steps climb up to the hall. The sound of distant water comes from behind the walls.␀A stone slab seals the eastern crawlway. Its arch contains a narrow coin slot. An inscription promises passage to anyone paying the keeper's toll. The cellar is south.␀Faded portraits watch a brass-locked vault door to the east. Mechanical footsteps echo from a guardroom north. The crypt is west.␀A stone plinth stands under a dusty skylight. Its inscription reads 'The first treasure remembers the earth.' The vault's only exit is west.␀An ivy-covered wall shelters the garden. A broken ladder leads up to the clock tower. The orchard is east and the house south. An iron anchor could hold a climbing rope.␀A clock with an empty gear socket overlooks the garden below. A lens mount points at shutters overhead. A plaque reads: 'Time, tide and light open the way to the stars.'␀Cold ovens line the kitchen. The keeper's maintenance list mentions clock oil, a jammed pump and a hungry bird. The pantry is east; the hall is south.␀A dry pantry holds the last supplies left by the keeper. A battery wrapper promises another 120 turns of lamp light. The kitchen is west.␀Tools hang above a metal case secured with hexagonal bolts. A label inside its glass lid reads CLOCK GEAR. A chalk sketch shows a pump valve connected to the observatory. The cellar is east.␀Roots break through the orchard path. A greenhouse stands north. Old stone steps spiral down a dry well. The garden lies west.␀A raven guards a nest high in a dead vine. Something glassy catches the daylight beneath its claws. The orchard is south.␀Stone steps climb to the orchard above. A rotted satchel rests in the silt. The keeper's initials are stitched into it. A low tunnel heads east toward the waterworks.␀Every footstep answers itself in the dark. A pipe runs north toward the pump room. The well lies west. A scratched arrow labels the pipe: 'Tide engine - service with wrench.'␀A pump shudders against a loose housing. A wheel valve is closed beside it. The tunnel is south; a walkway follows the pipe east to the reservoir.␀Black water covers the northern causeway to a shrine. A pipe leads west to the pump room. Iron stairs climb up to a bridge of gears. A gauge shows the water level is dangerously high.␀A narrow causeway leads south over the drained reservoir. Shells surround a stone altar. 'The second treasure remembers the sea,' reads a band of worn copper.␀A clockwork warden patrols the way east to a bridge. Its joints screech with every step. The gallery is south. The warden's chest plate bears the words SERVICE WITH OIL.␀Brass teeth turn far below the bridge. The guardroom is west, a crystal mine north. Stairs descend to the reservoir. A faded warning recommends music when passing the warden.␀Quartz gleams in the walls. A jewelled survey marker lies among the old workings. This forgotten reward is outside the keeper's three-treasure quest. The bridge is south.␀The keeper's ghost stands among sealed folios. It searches empty pockets as if something has been lost. A music stand faces the door south to the library.␀The dome is open. A crown waits inside a glass star case. A riddle asks: 'I end the night and begin the day. Name me.' The tower stair descends beneath the telescope.␀lamp␀key␀coin␀idol␀rope␀bread␀oil␀wrench␀gear␀lens␀chalice␀crown␀gem␀journal␀flute␀battery␀An electric lamp. Its charge lasts 160 lit turns; one spare battery adds 120.␀A brass key, stamped with the same crest as the gallery's vault lock.␀A silver toll coin. The crypt's slot looks just wide enough to accept it.␀A jade idol with soil caught in its carving. Return it to the cabinet outside.␀A long climbing rope. Secure it to the garden's iron anchor with USE ROPE.␀A surprisingly intact loaf. A hungry bird might part with its prize for this.␀A refillable oil can. There is enough for the tower clock and the warden.␀A heavy wrench. Its jaws match the workshop case bolts and the pump housing.␀A brass clock gear. It fits the empty socket in the tower's mechanism.␀A telescope lens. The tower has an empty mount below the observatory shutters.␀A silver chalice, cool with sea spray. Return it to the cabinet outside.␀A star crown, the keeper's last treasure. Return it to the cabinet outside.␀A ruby survey marker. It is an optional treasure for the cabinet outside.␀The keeper's journal. READ JOURNAL reveals its story; the ghost may want it back.␀A little flute. Its lullaby can quiet the clockwork warden for a few turns.␀A single-use lamp battery. USE BATTERY works even when your lamp is empty.␀north␀east␀south␀west␀up␀down␀n␀e␀s␀w␀u␀d␀On a forgotten coast stands a house where the clocks have stopped. Its garden is wild, its halls are silent, and strange machinery sleeps beneath the stone.␀The keeper who tended this place has vanished. Only a restless ghost, a stubborn raven and a tireless brass guardian remain. Below them, buried passages lead toward black water and forgotten shrines.␀Recover the jade idol, silver chalice and star crown. Bring them home to the cabinet west of the house, and awaken the bond between earth, sea and stars.␀Explore with N, E, S, W, U and D. EXAMINE what you find and TALK to those you meet. JOURNAL follows your quest; HINT offers a nudge when the way is unclear.␀[␀[0m␀  ␀[0m[2J[H[?25l[?7l␀ZORK / CP-M␀ADVENTURE LOG␀N/E/S/W/U/D  X  TAKE  USE  GIVE  PUT  JOURNAL  HINT  HELP  Q␀Z O R K␀A Zork-inspired text adventure␀T H E   H O U S E   O F   T I D E S␀YOUR QUEST␀LISTEN. EXAMINE. EXPLORE.␀Press ENTER to begin   /   Q to return to CP/M␀An original text adventure inspired by Zork.␀It is too dark to see. Light your lamp or retrace your steps. Your compass and the stairs still work in the dark.␀Dawn shines on the awakened House of Tides. Its clock chimes above a flowing tide engine. The three treasures rest together in the cabinet, their long journey complete.␀The cabinet's carved crests glow around the treasures you have brought home. The house is east and the garden north. Its remaining treasures still wait.␀The stone slab has slid aside, revealing an eastern crawlway to the gallery. The cellar lies south. The toll coin has vanished into the ancient mechanism.␀The eastern vault door stands open. Portraits of the keeper's family line the way north to the guardroom. The crypt is west.␀A rope is secured beside the broken ladder. You can climb up to the tower, walk east to the orchard, or return south to the house.␀The clock ticks, water turns the tide engine, and your lens gathers the light. The shutters overhead are open: climb UP to the observatory, or DOWN to the garden.␀The repaired clock ticks steadily. A lens mount points at the shutters above. Time alone cannot open them: they also need running water and a lens.␀The clock's gear is fitted and its bearings are oiled. It waits to be wound. A lens mount points at the shutters above; the garden is below.␀The new gear fits the clock, but its dry bearings resist turning. An oil can would help. The dome is above the lens mount, the garden below.␀The clock's bearings are oiled, but a socket still awaits its missing gear. A lens mount points at the shutters above. The garden is below.␀The bolted case is open. A maintenance diagram links the tower clock, the pump valve and a telescope lens to the observatory. The cellar is east.␀The raven eats happily beside its nest. It has let go of the telescope lens. Broken panes admit shafts of sunlight. The orchard is south.␀The repaired pump hums and water surges through the open valve toward the tide engine. The reservoir is east, the tunnel south.␀The pump housing is secure. Its wheel valve remains closed, ready to be turned. The reservoir is east and the tunnel south.␀The water has fallen below the northern causeway. The shrine can now be reached. Iron stairs lead up to the bridge; the pump room is west.␀The keeper's ghost reads the returned journal with a quiet smile. A little music stand is near the sealed folios. The library is south.␀The star case stands open. Beyond the telescope, a pale dawn reaches across the sea. The clock tower lies down the winding stair.␀The warden salutes its new mechanic.␀The warden sleeps. Its gears will soon wake.␀The warden watches you. Do not linger without a plan.␀The warden paces across the eastern doorway.␀The ghost nods gratefully.␀The ghost whispers: 'My journal... lost in the well...'␀, ␀nothing loose␀nothing in the dark␀(blocked)␀[?25l␀SCORE:␀TURNS:␀LAMP:ON ␀LAMP:OFF ␀Darkness␀THE HOUSE OF TIDES   Treasures home: ␀/3␀You see: ␀Exits: ␀> ␀[?25h␀THE HOUSE OF TIDES␀Recover the idol, chalice and crown. PUT each IN the cabinet here.␀The keeper left clues. EXAMINE things, TALK to characters; try JOURNAL or HINT.␀A portrait's eyes seem to follow you.␀You cannot go that way.␀The slab blocks the crawlway. Examine the coin slot.␀The vault is locked. A brass key might fit.␀The ladder is unsafe. Secure a rope to the anchor first.␀The causeway is submerged. Repair the pump and open its valve.␀The warden bars the bridge. Oil its joints or lull it with music.␀The dome needs time: repair, oil and WIND the tower clock.␀The dome needs tide: restore the pump and open its valve.␀The dome needs light: fit a lens to the tower's telescope mount.␀You enter the darkness.␀light␀lantern␀spanner␀diary␀ruby␀Take what? Try TAKE LAMP.␀You already have it.␀It is too dark to find anything.␀You see no such thing within reach here.␀Taken.␀You are not carrying that.␀Dropped.␀Your lamp is not here.␀The lamp is empty. USE BATTERY, or return for the pantry's spare.␀The lamp is already lit.␀The lamp is already off.␀The lamp glows warmly.␀You switch off the lamp.␀door␀vault␀lock␀slot␀slab␀anchor␀ladder␀raven␀bird␀clock␀warden␀case␀bolts␀pump␀socket␀mount␀telescope␀ghost␀keeper␀Use what? Try USE KEY ON DOOR.␀That does not belong there.␀Bring your lamp here first.␀The lamp is fully charged.␀You fit the spare battery. The lamp gains 120 turns of charge.␀You need light to do that.␀The vault is already open.␀The key turns. The vault door swings open.␀The crawlway is already open.␀The coin drops into the slot. The slab opens an eastern crawlway.␀You secure the rope. It is now safe to climb UP to the tower.␀The gear case is already open.␀The bolts loosen. You open the case and reveal a clock gear.␀The pump housing is already secure.␀You tighten the pump housing. Now TURN VALVE to start the water.␀The gear settles into the socket. The clock still needs oil and winding.␀The clock is already oiled.␀Oil frees the clock's bearings. A fitted gear and WIND CLOCK will set it going.␀The warden's joints are already running smoothly.␀You oil the warden. Its blade lowers; it salutes and welcomes its mechanic.␀The raven trades its prize for your loaf. A glass lens drops into the moss.␀The lens clicks into the telescope mount. Light reaches the dome mechanism.␀The ghost reads its lost journal. 'Now I remember. I can finally leave.'␀It gives you a flute: 'My warden still remembers this lullaby.'␀The warden is already peaceful.␀The lullaby stills the warden. You have a few turns to pass.␀You cannot use that here.␀crawlway␀The star case is already open.␀The case listens for the answer to its riddle. SAY your answer.␀There is nothing like that to open here.␀You need light to work the mechanism.␀valve␀The loose pump would burst. Repair its housing first.␀The valve is already open.␀You turn the valve. The reservoir drains and the tide engine begins to turn.␀The clock needs its missing gear and oil before it can be wound.␀The clock is already ticking.␀You wind the clock. Its first chime in a hundred years rings across the house.␀There is no such mechanism to operate here.␀The treasure cabinet is outside, west of the house.␀The cabinet holds the idol, chalice, crown and optional gem.␀You are not carrying that treasure.␀The jade idol settles into the cabinet. Its earth crest shines green.␀The silver chalice rests beside the sea crest. It glows like moonlit water.␀The star crown fills the cabinet's last great hollow. Tiny stars begin to burn.␀You add the mine's ruby to the cabinet, an unexpected gift for the keeper.␀nothing␀You are carrying: ␀Idol: safely home in the cabinet.␀Idol: in your pack, ready to return home.␀Idol: the gallery vault is open.␀Idol: follow the cellar's silver toll to the brass-locked vault.␀Chalice: safely home in the cabinet.␀Chalice: in your pack, ready to return home.␀Chalice: the reservoir causeway is clear; seek the northern shrine.␀Chalice: the waterworks need a repaired pump and an open valve.␀Crown: safely home in the cabinet.␀Crown: in your pack, ready to return home.␀Crown: the star case is open.␀Crown: time, tide and light open the dome; a spoken answer opens the case.␀YOUR QUEST: bank the idol, chalice and crown in the cabinet outside.␀Tower: the keeper's clock is ticking.␀Tower: recover the workshop gear, oil the clock, then wind it.␀Light: the telescope lens is fitted.␀Light: a raven in the greenhouse guards something glassy.␀Keeper: the ghost has found its memories.␀Optional: the archive's ghost seeks a journal lost in the well.␀The mine's gem is optional. Bank it before completing the three-treasure quest.␀A lamp hangs in the entrance hall. Take it before going below.␀Recover the journal at the bottom of the orchard's well, then GIVE JOURNAL TO GHOST.␀A loaf from the pantry might persuade the raven. GIVE BREAD TO RAVEN.␀USE OIL ON WARDEN for lasting peace, or PLAY FLUTE for a short lullaby.␀The wrench in this room fits the case bolts. OPEN CASE.␀Take the cellar's silver coin and USE COIN ON SLOT.␀The library's brass key fits the vault door.␀USE WRENCH ON PUMP before you TURN VALVE.␀Fit the workshop gear, oil the clock with the kitchen's oil, then WIND CLOCK.␀What ends the night and begins the day? SAY DAWN.␀The crypt's coin slot leads to the first treasure. Seek a silver coin below the hall.␀The idol lies behind the gallery's brass lock; the key is in the library.␀Descend the orchard's well. The tunnel reaches a pump: repair it and turn the valve.␀The tower's dome needs a ticking clock, running water and a fitted telescope lens.␀Carry the three main treasures home and PUT each IN CABINET. JOURNAL tracks the other tasks.␀Move: N E S W U D, GO NORTH, CLIMB UP. LOOK / L redraws the room.␀Objects: TAKE KEY, DROP KEY, USE KEY ON DOOR, OPEN CASE.␀Discover: EXAMINE / X, READ, SEARCH, TALK TO GHOST, HINT, JOURNAL.␀Interact: GIVE BREAD TO RAVEN, WIND CLOCK, TURN VALVE, PLAY FLUTE.␀Light: LIGHT LAMP, EXTINGUISH LAMP, USE BATTERY. I lists your items.␀Bank treasures: PUT IDOL IN CABINET or DEPOSIT ALL, outside the house.␀SAY an answer; WAIT lets time pass. SCORE, RESTART, QUIT / Q.␀Only successful actions cost turns. Looking, talking and hints are free.␀The keeper wrote: 'I linked the dome to time, tide and focused light.'␀'The clock needs a gear and oil. The pump must be mended before its valve opens.'␀'If the star case forgets me, I shall speak DAWN. Let the three treasures come home.'␀The last page asks that this journal be returned to its owner in the archive.␀It is too dark to examine that.␀note␀notes␀table␀shelves␀'Silver opens the crypt. Brass opens the vault. Time, tide and light open the dome.'␀Another note says the keeper disappeared while inspecting the orchard's well.␀The eastern crawlway is open.␀The slot accepts a silver coin. Try USE COIN ON SLOT.␀The vault door is open.␀The brass lock matches the library's key.␀The clock gear's case is open.␀Hexagonal bolts hold the case shut. A wrench would fit.␀The rope now makes the tower climb safe.␀A rope tied to the iron anchor would make the ladder safe.␀plaque␀The clock's gear is in place.␀The clock has an empty gear socket. Search the workshop's case.␀Its bearings have been oiled.␀The bearings are dry. There may be oil in the kitchen.␀The clock is ticking.␀Once the gear and oil are ready, WIND CLOCK.␀shutters␀A mount takes a glass lens. The dome interlock also needs the clock and the waterworks.␀nest␀The raven has traded its glass prize for bread.␀The raven's nest contains a lens. A hungry bird may accept bread.␀The housing is secure. The wheel valve controls the flow.␀The housing is loose. Tighten it with a wrench before opening the valve.␀The valve is open and the tide engine has water.␀The wheel valve is closed. TURN VALVE once the pump is safe.␀riddle␀The star case is open.␀'I end the night and begin the day. Name me.' SAY your answer.␀cabinet␀The cabinet accepts the idol, chalice, crown and optional mine gem. PUT a treasure IN CABINET.␀satchel␀The rotted satchel holds the keeper's journal, still dry inside its cover.␀Its joints need oil. A chest plate also describes a musical sleep override.␀You find no further clue in that here.␀'I was checking the well when I lost everything. My journal knows what I no longer can.'␀'Please bring it back. I once played a flute to calm my guardian.'␀'Thank you. The star case opens to DAWN. Bring our treasures home.'␀'The oil can will make my warden gentle. The flute can put it briefly to sleep.'␀'Mechanic recognised. Bridge access granted. Thank you for the oil.'␀'Maintenance overdue. Oil required. Unauthorised visitors will be escorted out.'␀The raven croaks a satisfied thank-you.␀The raven croaks: 'Bread! Bread!' and grips the glass prize.␀No one here answers you.␀The warden wakes and resumes its patrol.␀The warden raises its blade. Act soon, or retreat south.␀The warden gently escorts you back to the gallery. Your belongings are safe.␀Your lamp goes out. Fit the pantry's battery if you still have it.␀Your lamp is growing dim: twenty lit turns remain.␀Earth, sea and stars shine together. The house's windows fill with dawn.␀The keeper steps into the sunlight, smiles, and is finally at peace.␀A grateful whisper rises from the archive. One story still waits to be told.␀YOU HAVE WON! Press ENTER to return to CP/M.␀the␀a␀brass␀silver␀jade␀glass␀star␀clockwork␀talk␀to␀look␀l␀at␀on␀in␀into␀with␀Try a command such as USE KEY ON DOOR or GIVE JOURNAL TO GHOST.␀Please name one object and, if needed, one target.␀use␀give␀put␀deposit␀feed␀That command does not take a second object.␀go␀Go where? Use NORTH, EAST, SOUTH, WEST, UP or DOWN.␀It is too dark to see.␀help␀?␀inventory␀i␀quests␀hint␀score␀The maximum is 300: exploration, first finds, solved puzzles and banked treasures.␀quit␀q␀Goodbye, adventurer.␀restart␀wait␀z␀Time passes. The house creaks.␀take␀get␀all␀Nothing loose is within reach.␀drop␀The raven wants bread.␀play␀extinguish␀That is not a lamp.␀open␀unlock␀turn␀wind␀repair␀Examine the mechanism to learn what it needs.␀Treasures belong in the cabinet outside.␀You have no treasures to deposit here.␀say␀Your word echoes through the house.␀dawn␀daybreak␀sunrise␀The word DAWN lights the stars on the case. Its glass lid opens.␀The stars flicker, but the case stays shut. Read its riddle.␀examine␀x␀read␀search␀climb␀Use UP or DOWN at a stair or a safe ladder.␀I do not understand. Type HELP for commands.␀Your journey can wait. Goodbye, adventurer.␀[?7h[?25h␀
